#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# subgroup_index

#% text
# `subgroup_index(G, H)`: the index of the subgroup H in G (G a permutation or finitely presented group)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a finitely presented group the subgroup is given by words and its index is found by coset enumeration.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
subgroup_index(symmetric_group(4), dihedral_group(4))
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
subgroup_index(finitely_presented_group([a, b], [a^2, b^3, table([a, b], 5)]), [a])
#% output
#= 30

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `group_order`, `right_coset_representatives`, `coset_table`
